Third-party code and assets in this repository
==============================================

The MIT license in LICENSE covers only the original work in this fork. Everything
below was copied, vendored, ported or derived from someone else and keeps its own
terms. Entries are ordered from "no open-source license" to "permissive".


1. dicekeys/dicekeys-app-ios  (the app this fork started from)
--------------------------------------------------------------
Origin:    https://github.com/dicekeys/dicekeys-app-ios, commit 543a1b0 (v0.73)
Owner:     DiceKeys, LLC
License:   NONE GRANTED. Upstream's LICENSE.md reads, in full:

    This project is currently copyright DiceKeys, LLC with all rights reserved
    while we choose a license.

    We are choosing between the MIT license, under which we have already
    released our seeded crypto libraries, and a candidate "Right to Privacy"
    open source license that forbids the use of this code in such applications
    as stalkerware and government surveillance. [...] If you have thoughts on
    this choice, please contribute them either to the repository for the
    candidate license or by email us at license@dicekeys.com.

Where in this repo:
    DiceKeys/Model/DiceKey, DiceKeys/Model/Recipes, DiceKeys/Model/BIP39,
    DiceKeys/Services/Api, the illustrations in
    DiceKeys/Resources/Assets.xcassets, the app-icon mark
    (scripts/app-icon-source/original-mark-1024.png and everything generated
    from it), and the UI flows in DiceKeys/Features (rewritten, but derived).
    GitHub's terms let a public repository be forked and
    viewed; they do not grant a license to redistribute. This fork is therefore
    for personal use (local builds, TestFlight to the owner's devices), not for
    publication, until DiceKeys, LLC chooses a license.


2. dicekeys/read-dicekey  (the DiceKey scanner)
-----------------------------------------------
Origin:    https://github.com/dicekeys/read-dicekey, commit 0440036
Owner:     DiceKeys, LLC
License:   NONE GRANTED (same placeholder as above).
Where in this repo:
    Packages/DiceKeysCore/Sources/ReadDiceKey is a Swift port of upstream's
    lib-read-dicekey (same algorithm, stage by stage; see
    docs/SCANNER-PORT-NOTES.md), so it is a derivative work.
    Packages/DiceKeysCore/Sources/ReadDiceKey/OcrFontTables.swift is generated
    from upstream's rasterized Inconsolata glyph tables (item 7).
    Packages/DiceKeysCore/Tests/ReadDiceKeyTests/Fixtures/images/*.jpg|png are
    upstream's 23 test photographs, and Fixtures/reference-cpp-scanner.json is
    upstream's scanner output on them.


